(D3 - Discrepancy 3 repro: a negative MILLISECOND duration never returns.
 `Wait -5 milliseconds.` divides the count by 1000 with an UNSIGNED
 divide (coreasm/x86_64/time.asm, SLEEP_MILLISECONDS), so -5 becomes
 18446744073709551611 milliseconds and tv_sec becomes about 1.8e16
 seconds - roughly 585 million years. The seconds spelling of the same
 nonsense returns at once (TIM-51.vox), because a negative tv_sec is
 rejected by the kernel rather than reinterpreted.
 `print "the wait returned".` never runs, so the program prints nothing.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D3.vox -o p && timeout 10 ./p
 expected output:
   (no output: the program is still sleeping when the 10-second harness
   timeout fires, so the recorded outcome is exit 124. Not a crash and not
   a busy loop - a sleep nobody will outlive.)
   exit 124
)
Wait -5 milliseconds.
print "the wait returned".
